- PPMd7 / PPMdH shared codec (`src/compress/ppmd.rs` and
  `src/compress/ppmd/**`)
  - Original reference: the PPMd implementation shipped within the 7-Zip
    project, as documented in files such as `Ppmd.h`, `Ppmd7.c`,
    `Ppmd7Dec.c`, and `Ppmd7Enc.c`
  - Rust-side basis: `ppmd-rust` crate (https://crates.io/crates/ppmd-rust)
  - Upstream port license: CC0-1.0 OR MIT-0
  - Repository scope: port of that upstream PPMd7 model (structure and
    constants carried over), adapted to this crate's `no_std + alloc`
    style and 7z method integration and ZIP method 98 (PPMd)

- ZPAQ (`src/compress/zpaq/**`, `src/archive/zpaq/**`)
  - Reference and port source: Matt Mahoney's ZPAQ format, context-mixing
    model, and ZPAQL VM (`zpaq`/`libzpaq` v7.15, released to the public
    domain; the bundled upstream `libdivsufsort-lite` (MIT), libtomcrypt
    AES, and Salsa20/8 (both public domain) components are not used by
    this port). The written specification "ZPAQ Level 1
    and Level 2" (zpaq206.pdf, https://mattmahoney.net/dc/zpaq206.pdf) is
    text-extractable, but tables and superscripts degrade under
    extraction, so the spec's own reference implementation was used as
    the authoritative source for the predictor state table,
    squash/stretch tables, built-in level 1-3 model blobs, and arithmetic
    coder semantics (the IMPLEMENTATION_POLICY exception for written-spec
    portions lacking usable precision, with a clean rights chain).
  - libzpaq was also compiled locally (interpreter path, -DNOJIT) as a
    development oracle: bidirectional encode/decode compatibility was
    verified for modeled levels 1-3, unmodeled (n=0) stored streams,
    PASS and PROG (PCOMP) segments, empty/binary/large/random payloads,
    and multi-segment archives. Upstream-generated fixtures are committed
    under `tests/fixtures/zpaq/`; the oracle harness lives under
    `.local/refs/libzpaq/` (gitignored).
  - JIDAC journaling support (`src/archive/zpaq/jidac.rs`) was written
    against the journaling code in upstream `zpaq.cpp` v7.15 (block
    naming `jDC<date><type><num>`, transaction layout c/d/h/i, global
    fragment table, deletion records, content-defined fragmenting with
    the order-1 rolling hash and SHA-1 fragment reuse). The upstream
    `zpaq` CLI (v7.15, installed in the test container via `pkg/zpaq`)
    was used as a bidirectional oracle: it decodes this crate's JIDAC
    output including `JidacAppender` incremental transactions
    (`zpaq l`/`zpaq x`/`zpaq a` append) and this crate decodes
    CLI-produced multi-transaction archives including deletions and
    fragment-dedup reuse. The same CLI also serves as the file-based
    fuzz oracle (`ArchiveSpec::Zpaq`) for `original-compress` and
    `original-decompress` patterns.
  - Patent note: upstream explicitly states the format is "not encumbered
    by any patents or pending patents" and that all past versions were
    published to establish prior art (zpaq.html)
  - The config-language compiler (`src/compress/zpaq/config.rs`) ports
    upstream `libzpaq.cpp` `Compiler` (public domain): the `.cfg`
    grammar — `comp`/`hcomp`/`pcomp` sections, ZPAQL mnemonics, the
    `if`/`else`/`endif` and `do`/`while`/`until`/`forever` structured
    pseudo-operations lowering to `jt`/`jf`/`jmp`/`lj`, and `$N+M`
    argument substitution — is defined only by that implementation, so
    it is used as the normative source under the IMPLEMENTATION_POLICY
    exception. Fidelity is pinned by compiling upstream's own `mid.cfg`
    and `max.cfg` (zpaq 1.07+ distribution text; the GPL license notice
    and per-line annotations are stripped — the descriptive comment
    fragment `zpaq 1.07+ config file ...` remains, and the retained
    declarations are byte-equivalent to the public-domain libzpaq
    built-in model blobs; even if the retained text were GPL-3.0 it is
    combinable into AGPL-3.0 under GPL-3.0 section 13) plus a
    reconstructed `min.cfg`, all byte-exact against the built-in
    level 1-3 model blobs.
  - Repository scope: wire-compatible low-level codec (including
    optional encoder-side PCOMP/PROG emission via CustomModel), the
    config-language compiler, a multi-entry archive layer with
    crate-local journaling, and upstream JIDAC journaling streams
    (decode, single-transaction emit, and incremental append with
    content-defined fragmenting and SHA-1 deduplication)


